# Railway Environment Variables Template
# Copy these to your Railway service settings

# ============================================
# DATABASE (PostgreSQL Service)
# ============================================
# Automatically provided by Railway when you add PostgreSQL
# Use the reference syntax to connect services
DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}

# ============================================
# API SERVICE VARIABLES
# ============================================

# JWT Configuration
JWT_SECRET=change-this-to-a-secure-random-string
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d

# API Configuration
API_PORT=3001

# Cloudinary (Image Upload Service)
# Sign up at https://cloudinary.com/ for free tier
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your-cloud-name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your-api-key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your-api-secret

# ============================================
# CRAWLER SERVICE VARIABLES
# ============================================

# Crawler Configuration
CRAWLER_SCHEDULE=0 */6 * * *
CRAWLER_USER_AGENT=WhatsUpAddis/1.0

# ============================================
# NOTES
# ============================================
#
# 1. Generate a secure JWT_SECRET:
#    openssl rand -hex 32
#
# 2. DATABASE_URL reference:
#    Use ${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}} to automatically
#    reference the PostgreSQL service in your project
#
# 3. Service references:
#    ${{ServiceName.VARIABLE}} - Reference another service
#    ${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}} - Database connection string
#
# 4. Railway automatically provides:
#    - PORT: The port your service should listen on
#    - RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT: current environment (production, staging, etc)
#    - RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN: public URL of your service
#    - RAILWAY_PRIVATE_DOMAIN: internal URL for service-to-service communication
#
# 5. How to set variables:
#
#    Via Dashboard:
#    - Go to service → Variables tab
#    - Click "New Variable"
#    - Add key-value pairs
#
#    Via CLI:
#    railway variables set KEY=VALUE --service service-name
#
# 6. Environments:
#    Railway supports multiple environments (production, staging, etc)
#    Variables can be environment-specific
